  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Survey the forest for repeated structural patterns and codify them as Forester templates in <html:code>templates/</html:code>. The goal is to reduce friction when creating common tree types.</html:p>
    <html:p>Approach: browse existing trees looking for recurring frontmatter combinations, content shapes, and metadata conventions. For each pattern, decide whether it warrants a dedicated template.</html:p>
    <html:p>Known candidate: <html:strong>advisor-meeting</html:strong> — typed or handwritten notes from a meeting with Max, tagged <html:code>meeting</html:code> and <html:code>advisor-meeting</html:code> with taxon <html:code>Journal</html:code>. Creating this template is a separate follow-on task.</html:p>
